    {#
      ======================================================================
      HOME PAGE

      TEN SECTIONS, AND NO TWO OF THEM ARE BUILT THE SAME WAY. The page this
      replaces was five variations on "eyebrow, big heading, grid of cards",
      which made every screen read like the one before it. Each section here
      has one job, and a structure only it uses. The reasoning for each is in
      homepage.css, next to the rules that draw it, along with the argument for
      the running order.

      ROUTING SITS THIRD, one screen from the fold, because on a page selling
      systems that cost seven figures the visitor almost always arrives already
      knowing something has to be sorted. The positioning statement reads
      better after the five questions than in front of them: by then it is
      answering "why does this have to be done properly" rather than opening
      with it.

      THREE OF THE TEN ARE THE SITE'S OWN COMPONENTS, unchanged and included
      rather than reimplemented: the coverage map that closes /about/ and every
      service page, the filmstrip from /about/, and the enquiry drawer the
      whole site shares. A homepage that drew its own map or its own photo band
      would be a second answer to a question the site already answers once.

      THERE IS NO DEDICATED EMERGENCY SECTION, and that is deliberate. The
      number is already persistent on every screen: the sticky bar carries it
      above 900px, the floating dock carries it below, the hero states it in
      full, and the footer repeats it. An 88px billboard of it in the middle of
      the page was the one block here saying a fifth time what nothing on the
      page lets you miss.

      THE FOOTER CTA IS TURNED OFF ON THIS PAGE (hideFooterCta above), and
      that is not an oversight: section 9 IS that call to action, word for
      word, and with both on the page the same heading and the same paragraph
      appeared twice within one screen of each other. The footer itself is
      untouched.

      THE TOOLTIP COMPONENT is new and site-wide capable, but adopted HERE
      ONLY for now: /styles/components/tooltip.css and /scripts/tooltip.js.
      Other pages pick it up as their copy is revisited, one page at a time.
      Its usage rules (never in a heading, two terms per paragraph maximum,
      first occurrence on the page only) are applied throughout below.
      ======================================================================
    #}

    {#
      Organization + LocalBusiness, IN THE BODY RATHER THAN THE HEAD, because
      base.njk owns <head> and is shared by every page. JSON-LD is valid and
      indexed anywhere in the document, so the placement costs nothing.

      FOLLOW-UP: base.njk already emits a minimal LocalBusiness on every page.
      Both nodes describe the same business, so give that one the same @id as
      the node below and the two merge into one instead of reading as two
      businesses at one address. That edit belongs to a shared-layout task,
      not to this page.
    #}
    <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@graph": [
        {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "@id": "{{ site.url }}/#organization",
          "name": "{{ site.name }}",
          "legalName": "{{ site.legalName }}",
          "url": "{{ site.url }}/",
          "telephone": "{{ site.tel }}",
          "email": "{{ site.email }}",
          "description": "Bespoke water treatment, private water supplies, chlorination and water hygiene compliance for estates, plant and commercial facilities across Surrey, Sussex and the South East.",
          "address": {
            "@type": "PostalAddress",
            "streetAddress": "{{ site.address.street }}",
            "addressLocality": "{{ site.address.locality }}",
            "addressRegion": "{{ site.address.region }}",
            "postalCode": "{{ site.address.postcode }}",
            "addressCountry": "GB"
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "LocalBusiness",
          "@id": "{{ site.url }}/#localbusiness",
          "parentOrganization": { "@id": "{{ site.url }}/#organization" },
          "name": "{{ site.name }}",
          "url": "{{ site.url }}/",
          "telephone": "{{ site.tel }}",
          "email": "{{ site.email }}",
          "priceRange": "££",
          "address": {
            "@type": "PostalAddress",
            "streetAddress": "{{ site.address.street }}",
            "addressLocality": "{{ site.address.locality }}",
            "addressRegion": "{{ site.address.region }}",
            "postalCode": "{{ site.address.postcode }}",
            "addressCountry": "GB"
          },
          "areaServed": [{% for c in maps.counties %}{ "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "{{ c }}" }{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}]
        }
      ]
    }
    </script>

